#, python-brace-format
msgid "**Declared per application, literally.** Every consumer role declares `stack: {enabled: true, shared: true}` in its own `meta/services.yml`. The values are fixed literals, not `'<role>' in group_names` expressions. A central per-category declaration and the `add_host` injection used for OpenResty were rejected."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Decommission:** On a compose deploy without `--id` and with `CLEANUP`, the destructor stops every compose instance directly below `DIR_COMPOSITIONS` that no active role owns with `compose down --remove-orphans` and then deletes it, before `sys-service-terminator` starts the deferred services and the CLI tests run. The instance's named volumes stay; bind-mounted data inside the directory, such as `volumes/`, goes with it. A role counts as active when any host of the inventory carries it, when it is in the `CURRENT_PLAY_APPLICATIONS` dependency closure, or when the play prepared its instance. Only a directory named after a known role and carrying the full instance layout (`compose.yml`, `.env/`, `config/`, `services/`, `volumes/`) counts as an instance. An instance that a container outside its compose project is named after, such as a launcher-managed container, stays too. Every directory left alone is listed in the deploy output. The deploy fails before deleting anything when a container still carries the stopped project's name or working directory. A failure of the decommission, the deferred services or the CLI tests still unlocks the timers and fails the deploy."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Decommission:** On a compose deploy without ``--id`` and with ``CLEANUP``, the destructor stops every compose instance directly below ``DIR_COMPOSITIONS`` that no active role owns with ``compose down --remove-orphans`` and then deletes it, before ``sys-service-terminator`` starts the deferred services and the CLI tests run. The instance’s named volumes stay; bind-mounted data inside the directory, such as ``volumes/``, goes with it. A role counts as active when any host of the inventory carries it, when it is in the ``CURRENT_PLAY_APPLICATIONS`` dependency closure, or when the play prepared its instance. Only a directory named after a known role and carrying the full instance layout (``compose.yml``, ``.env/``, ``config/``, ``services/``, ``volumes/``) counts as an instance. An instance that a container outside its compose project is named after, such as a launcher-managed container, stays too. Every directory left alone is listed in the deploy output. The deploy fails before deleting anything when a container still carries the stopped project’s name or working directory. A failure of the decommission, the deferred services or the CLI tests still unlocks the timers and fails the deploy."
msgstr ""

