msgstr "**`hugo` Hesabatlı məlumat / modul hataları**: upstream depozit bir klassik və ya Hugo Modul axtarır. Pin tanınmış-good tag `source_version`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**`images/`** opts into NFS (`nfs: true` in the `compose_volumes` call from `templates/compose.yml.j2`). The volume is shared across all swarm nodes so the MediaWiki application service can be rescheduled freely."
msgstr "**`images/`** NFS daxil olmaq (`nfs: true` the `compose_volumes` Bakı `templates/compose.yml.j2`). MediaWiki proqram xidmətinin mediaWiki proqram xüsusiyyətləri arasında həyata keçirilir."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**`infinito-i18n-libretranslate`**: model weights; downloading them again needs an `allowed_domains` entry. High risk."
msgstr "**`infinito-i18n-libretranslate`**: model ağırları; onları yenidən yükləyin `allowed_domains` giriş. Yüksək risk."

msgid "**`ldap`:** `enable-login-with-ldap`, the \"LDAP\" button on the login form that binds against [`svc-db-openldap`](../svc-db-openldap/). Under SSO it is off and LDAP accounts sign in through the Keycloak federation."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**`linux.sh`**. installs the CA into the Linux system trust store"
msgstr "**`linux.sh`**. CA-yı Linux sistemi əməliyyat mağazalarına yükləyin"

msgid "**`local.sh` — fully local, no external GitHub.** Checks the runner containers are healthy and the DooD socket works, then `container cp`s the repo into a runner, **builds the Infinito image locally**, and deploys `web-app-dashboard` (all other services disabled) inside a **sealed, throwaway Docker daemon** that shares the runner's network namespace. The sandbox is torn down on exit, so the host stack is never touched and **no GitHub/GHCR access is required**. On the update pass the heavy deploy is skipped (it is validated once on the first pass)."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**`mechanism: bridge`** marks an addon that *is* a network/appservice bridge to an external system (e.g. a Matrix `mautrix` bridge to WhatsApp)."
msgstr "**`mechanism: bridge`** bir addon tapmaq *Axtarış* bir şəhər/appservice körpü xarici sistemdə (e.g. bir Matrix `mautrix` WhatsApp)."

msgid "**`native`:** `enable-login-with-password` or `disable-login-with-password`. Penpot keeps the email and password fields for the LDAP button, but without this flag no local password signs in. When it is on, `tasks/main.yml` bootstraps a local password for the `administrator` profile through the backend PREPL (`create-profile` for a fresh profile, `update-profile` when a federated login already created it)."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**`no_remote_surface` (24):** `svc-ai-ollama`, `svc-ai-robot`, `web-app-chess`, `web-app-dashboard`, `web-app-fediwall`, `web-app-hugo`, `web-app-littlejs`, `web-app-mig`, `web-app-mini-qr`, `web-app-navigator`, `web-app-roulette-wheel`, `web-app-sphinx`, `web-opt-rdr-domains`, `web-opt-rdr-www`, `web-svc-asset`, `web-svc-cdn`, `web-svc-coturn`, `web-svc-design`, `web-svc-file`, `web-svc-html`, `web-svc-legal`, `web-svc-logout`, `web-svc-mirror`, `web-svc-simpleicons`. These roles have no independently useful authenticated remote action contract at the pinned implementation. Static published content MAY later be consumed through one owning application's bounded `resource_readonly` adapter, but a new MCP sidecar that merely reimplements a static site's behavior does not count as integration. Model tool calling in Ollama does not by itself make Ollama an MCP client or server."
