msgid "A provider declares ``overlay.stream_relay`` with a ``switch`` and the ``ports`` it opens. While the switch is true and the reverse proxy's own overlay applies in the mode, the provider and the reverse proxy share ``<entity>-relay`` and nothing else does, so the relay never puts the proxy on the provider's overlay with its consumers."
msgstr ""

msgid "A provider declares `overlay.stream_relay` in its `meta/networks.yml` with a `switch` (a config path on the provider), the `ports` it relays and the `subnet` of the relay network. While the switch is true, and only in the modes where the reverse proxy (`svc-prx-openresty`) itself runs on overlays (its own `networks.overlay.modes`, today `[swarm]`), the provider and the reverse proxy join a dedicated network `<entity>-relay` (`openldap-relay`), and no other role joins it. The provider carries its entity name as alias there. The reverse proxy never joins the provider's overlay. In compose openresty keeps the host network and reaches the published loopback port as before."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
