msgid "No Playwright scenario gates on `ldap`, and [`templates/playwright.env.j2`](./templates/playwright.env.j2) suppresses the service-gate check for `LDAP_SERVICE_ENABLED`. Shopware has no LDAP sign-in of its own and the role installs no admin-LDAP extension, so there is no LDAP-bind surface to drive: with `sso` on, directory accounts reach the administration through Keycloak's user federation and the AdminOpenAuth provider, which [`files/playwright/test-rbac.js`](./files/playwright/test-rbac.js) covers; with `sso` off, no directory account reaches Shopware."
msgstr ""

msgid "No Playwright scenario gates on `ldap`, and [services.yml](./meta/services.yml) exempts the flag from the Playwright service-flag check. The indexer configures LDAP only as `ldap_authz_domain`, which adds `backend_roles` to a user Keycloak or `internal_users.yml` already authenticated, so the stack has no LDAP-bind login to drive: with `sso` on every directory account signs in through Keycloak, which [files/playwright/test-rbac-roles.js](./files/playwright/test-rbac-roles.js) covers, and with `sso` off only the internal `admin` and `kibanaserver` accounts can sign in."
