msgid "[infinito-network-origins.php](infinito-network-origins.php) moves every site URL into the network the request's `Host` belongs to. `INFINITO_NETWORK_BASE_URLS` in [env.j2](../../templates/env.j2) lists the network siblings of each site, canonical network first, separated by `,`, and the sites by `;` (`WORDPRESS_NETWORK_BASE_URLS` in [vars/main.yml](../../vars/main.yml)). A URL whose host is a known site sibling is answered with that site's sibling in the request's network, for the `home` and `siteurl` options, `content_url`, `plugins_url`, `network_home_url`, `network_site_url` and `upload_dir`. `WP_CONTENT_URL` and `WP_PLUGIN_URL` are fixed from `siteurl` before any mu-plugin loads, which is why the URL filters are needed as well. The stored options keep the canonical URL, so WP-CLI and requests on any other host read them unchanged."
msgstr ""

