msgid "[x] The nft filter output and forward chains end in `drop`, and only reply-direction packets and flows this table marked skip the rules. The output chain accepts the node's own addresses, Tor's sockets (`skuid 0`, `skgid TOR_EGRESS_SOCKET_GID`), dnsmasq to its upstream, internal, non-routable, local IPv6, neighbour discovery and direct destinations; the forward chain jumps nowhere. The nat output chain redirects every remaining IPv4 TCP flow to the TransPort, and container traffic is redirected or dropped the same way. Proven on the rendered fragment by `test_all_fails_closed`, `test_only_flows_this_table_admitted_skip_the_rules`, `test_forwarded_ipv6_and_foreign_sources_meet_the_drop`, `test_neighbour_discovery_keeps_working` and `test_dns_leaves_only_from_dnsmasq_to_its_upstream`."
